.\" libmusiccast — mcctl(1)
.TH MCCTL 1 "@VERSION@" "libmusiccast" "Yamaha MusicCast control"
.SH NAME
mcctl \- control Yamaha MusicCast devices over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcctl
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.B detect
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.PP
.B mcctl
.B help
.PP
.B mcctl
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.B \-a
.I HOST
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
.B mcctl
.I HOST
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcctl
talks to Yamaha MusicCast speakers and receivers using the Yamaha Extended
Control (YXC) HTTP API on the local network.
.PP
Use
.B detect
to find devices via SSDP.
All other commands need a device
.IR HOST
(IP address or hostname), either as the first argument or with
.BR \-a .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address= HOST
Device IP address or hostname.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone= ZONE
Zone for zone commands (default:
.IR main ).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout= SEC
.SSD discovery wait time in seconds (default: 3).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output (e.g. show device ID in
.BR detect ).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-s ", " \-\-silent
Suppress stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-step= N
Step size for
.B volume up
and
.B volume down
(default: 1).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit (same as the
.B help
command).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Without a device address
.TP
.B detect
Search the LAN for MusicCast devices (SSDP).
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SS System queries
.TP
.B device-info
Device model, IDs, API version (\fIgetDeviceInfo\fR).
.TP
.B features
Capabilities and zone layout (\fIgetFeatures\fR).
.TP
.B zones
List zone IDs from
.BR features .
.TP
.B network-status
Network configuration (\fIgetNetworkStatus\fR).
.TP
.B func-status
Function status (\fIgetFuncStatus\fR).
.TP
.B location-info
Location / grouping (\fIgetLocationInfo\fR).
.TP
.B sound-program-list
Available sound programs (\fIgetSoundProgramList\fR).
.SS Zone commands
Zone is selected with
.BR \-z ;
default is
.IR main .
.TP
.B status
Zone status as JSON (\fIgetStatus\fR).
.TP
.B now-playing
Current input and track (\fIgetStatus\fR + \fIgetPlayInfo\fR for Net/USB, tuner, or CD).
Alias:
.BR playing .
.TP
.B power
Print power state (\fIon\fR or \fIstandby\fR).
.TP
.B power on\fR|\fBstandby\fR|\fBtoggle
Set power.
.TP
.B volume
Print current volume (and range when available).
.TP
.B volume \fIN\fR|\fBup\fR|\fBdown
Set volume or step up/down (use
.B \-\-step
with up/down).
.TP
.B mute
Print mute state (\fIon\fR = muted, \fIoff\fR = unmuted).
.TP
.B mute on\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBtoggle
Set mute.
.TP
.B input
Print the current input (\fIgetStatus\fR).
.TP
.B input list
List inputs the zone can select (\fIgetFeatures\fR \fIinput_list\fR).
.TP
.B input set \fIINPUT\fR
Select
.IR INPUT
(\fIsetInput\fR).
.I INPUT
must be one of the ids from
.BR "input list" .
.SS Playback
Acts on the source selected for the zone.
Net/USB and CD use
.IR setPlayback .
.B play
and
.B resume
both send
.IR play
(there is no separate resume request).
.B toggle
sends
.I play_pause
on Net/USB, and play or pause on CD based on the current state.
On the tuner,
.B next
and
.B previous
call
.I switchPreset ;
play, pause, and stop are not available for that input.
Line inputs (HDMI, aux, and similar) have no transport control.
.TP
.B play
.TP
.B resume
Start or resume playback.
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback.
.TP
.B stop
Stop playback.
.TP
.B toggle
Toggle between play and pause.
.TP
.B next
Next track, or the next tuner preset.
.TP
.B previous
.TP
.B prev
Previous track, or the previous tuner preset.
.SS Net/USB presets
Presets are shared across Net/USB sources (e.g. net radio, server).
.TP
.B preset list
List preset slots.
.TP
.B preset play \fIN
.TP
.B preset recall \fIN
Recall preset
.IR N
(switches input as needed).
.TP
.B preset store \fIN
Save currently playing Net/USB content to preset
.IR N .
.TP
.B preset clear \fIN
Clear preset
.IR N .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Discover devices:
.RS
.EX
mcctl detect
.EE
.RE
.TP
Power, volume, and input on the main zone:
.RS
.EX
mcctl -a 192.168.1.50 power on
mcctl -a living-room.local volume 45
mcctl -a living-room.local volume up --step 5
mcctl -a living-room.local input
mcctl -a living-room.local input list
mcctl -a living-room.local input set tuner
mcctl -a living-room.local pause
mcctl -a living-room.local next
.EE
.RE
.TP
Play Net/USB preset 3 on zone 2:
.RS
.EX
mcctl -a 192.168.1.50 -z zone2 preset play 3
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/include/musiccast.h
Library public API (libmusiccast).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg-config (1)
for
.BR libmusiccast .
.PP
Yamaha Extended Control API specifications (YXC Basic/Advanced).
.SH AUTHOR
Jasper Nevens
